/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 609 0 R
/T (To achieve best-in-class performance, companies must move beyond industry averages and embrace strategies that have been proven to deliver results. For instance, average adherence rates for chronic conditions typically range from 50-60%, while top-performing companies that implement real-time mentorship and patient support systems often achieve adherence rates closer to 75-80%. This improvement is driven by two main factors: the increased accessibility to care support through mentorship and the enhanced personal accountability created by patient support interventions, such as mentorship programs. These factors work together to make patients more likely to stay engaged with their treatment plans and adhere to recommended care.)
/E (To achieve best-in-class performance, companies must move beyond industry averages and embrace strategies that have been proven to deliver results. For instance, average adherence rates for chronic conditions typically range from 50-60%, while top-performing companies that implement real-time mentorship and patient support systems often achieve adherence rates closer to 75-80%. This improvement is driven by two main factors: the increased accessibility to care support through mentorship and the enhanced personal accountability created by patient support interventions, such as mentorship programs. These factors work together to make patients more likely to stay engaged with their treatment plans and adhere to recommended care.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
880 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 609 0 R
/T (Leading companies in the industry, such as Eli Lilly and Pfizer, have set new standards with initiatives like LillyDirect and PfizerForAll, which focus on direct-to-patient strategies. By adopting multi-channel patient engagement approaches, incorporating digital tools, personalized support, and mentorship programs, these companies have successfully achieved higher patient satisfaction and retention rates. Moreover, the shift toward direct-to-consumer \(DTC\) marketing has increased consumer sentiment and awareness around their treatment solutions. While specific data may vary, DTC marketing campaigns in the pharmaceutical industry often represent a significant portion of overall marketing spend, with estimates suggesting that DTC advertising budgets exceed $6 billion annually in the U.S. alone, according to data from the Kaiser Family Foundation. This investment has been shown to effectively boost brand awareness and patient engagement, helping companies to better connect with their target audiences.)
/E (Leading companies in the industry, such as Eli Lilly and Pfizer, have set new standards with initiatives like LillyDirect and PfizerForAll, which focus on direct-to-patient strategies. By adopting multi-channel patient engagement approaches, incorporating digital tools, personalized support, and mentorship programs, these companies have successfully achieved higher patient satisfaction and retention rates. Moreover, the shift toward direct-to-consumer \(DTC\) marketing has increased consumer sentiment and awareness around their treatment solutions. While specific data may vary, DTC marketing campaigns in the pharmaceutical industry often represent a significant portion of overall marketing spend, with estimates suggesting that DTC advertising budgets exceed $6 billion annually in the U.S. alone, according to data from the Kaiser Family Foundation. This investment has been shown to effectively boost brand awareness and patient engagement, helping companies to better connect with their target audiences.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [6]
>>
